> Unfortunately, [#17330](https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/pull/17330) does not fix this issue for me.

Can you try again?

Please try the following:
1. Write a minimal program that RA completions work in with an older bevy version. Please specify the bevy version (and rust version) that worked.
2. Share the line where the RA completions worked before but don't work with my PR anymore.
3. Please share the recursive expansion of the derive. In vscode this can be done with `CTRL+SHIFT+P` expand macro at cursor.

You may adapt the following program to cover your use case if you want:
```rust
#![allow(dead_code)]
use bevy::prelude::*;

#[derive(Component)]
struct MyComponent {
    value: f32,
}

//#[derive(Resource)]
struct MyResource {
    value: f32,
}
impl :<nick>::ecs::system::Resource for MyResource where Self: Send + Sync + 'static {}

fn hello_world(query: Query<&MyComponent>, resource: Res<MyResource>) {
    let component = query.iter().next().unwrap();
    let comp_value = component.value;
    let res_value_deref = resource.value;
    let res_value_direct = resource.into_inner().value;
    println!(
        "hello world! Value: {} {} {}",
        comp_value, res_value_deref, res_value_direct
    );
}

fn spawn_component(mut commands: Commands) {
    commands.spawn(MyComponent { value: 10.0 });
}

#[test]
fn simple_ecs_test() {
    App::new()
        .insert_resource(MyResource { value: 5.0 })
        .add_systems(Startup, spawn_component)
        .add_systems(Update, hello_world)
        .run();
}

```
